{%- comment -%}
  White background behind every product image (first image, variant images and the rest of the gallery), wherever it is shown (cards, product page,
  cart, menus, app blocks). Product images are transparent PNGs (product plus shadow), so without
  this they would take the colour of whatever section they sit on. Matches by file name, so it
  follows the images automatically when they are changed in admin.
  The product page gallery (main photos and thumbnails) is left out on purpose: there the theme's own
  background shows through.
  ponytail: Shopify loops stop at 50 items without paginate; the store has about 23 products.
  Past 50 products, move this into a paginated loop on a page that ignores ?page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture pib_rules -%}
  {%- for p in collections.all.products limit: 50 -%}
    {%- for pimg in p.images -%}
      {%- assign pib_file = pimg | image_url | split: '?' | first | split: '/' | last | replace: '"', '' -%}
      img[src*="/{{ pib_file }}"],
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign pib_rules = pib_rules | strip | remove_last: ',' -%}
{%- if pib_rules != blank -%}
  <style>{{ pib_rules }} { background-color: #fff !important; } .sp__gallery img, .sp__thumbs img { background-color: transparent !important; }</style>
{%- endif -%}
